   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to insurance reserve\nfunds of certain school districts",
    "basePrintNo": "S948",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S948-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-n, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S948\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to insurance\nreserve funds of certain school districts\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide that in the case of the Ithaca City School District, an\ninsurance reserve fund may be established and such school district may\nmake expenditures from such reserve fund for any loss, claim, action or\njudgment. for which the school district is authorized or required to\npurchase or maintain insurance.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of section 6-n of the general\nmunicipal law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn order to prudently manage the rising costs of health insurance, the\nIthaca City School District's (ICSD) Board of Education has elected to\nself-insure its health benefit program as of July 1, 2017.  Self-insu-\nrance offers many advantages for ICSD and its employees, however under\ncurrent law, school districts are prevented from retaining more than 4 E\nof their budget in an unappropriated fund balance. By authorizing ICSD\nto establish its own insurance reserve fund through this legislation, as\nexists for other school districts in the state, the District will be\nable to meet its duties of self-insurance. This essential tool will\nallow ICSD to manage year-to-year variability in claims.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018 - S7055A\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
